{"name":"Brick Yellow","hex":"#d2a161","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brick","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hardened rectangular block of mud, clay etc., used for building.","Such hardened mud, clay, etc. considered collectively, as a building material."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build, line, or form with bricks.","To make into bricks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brick"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brick","blocks":[{"text":"A brick is a type of building material used to build walls, pavements, and other elements in masonry construction. Properly, the term brick denotes a unit primarily composed of clay, but it is now also used informally to denote building units made of other materials or other chemically cured construction blocks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Brick.jpg/330px-Brick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brick","wikidata":"Q40089"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg/500px-Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg/1280px-Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg/500px-Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A wall constructed in glazed-headed Flemish bond brickwork pattern, with various shades and lengths","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrick_wall_close-up_view.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/%D9%86%D9%85%D8%A7%DB%8C_4.jpg/500px-%D9%86%D9%85%D8%A7%DB%8C_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/%D9%86%D9%85%D8%A7%DB%8C_4.jpg/1280px-%D9%86%D9%85%D8%A7%DB%8C_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/%D9%86%D9%85%D8%A7%DB%8C_4.jpg/500px-%D9%86%D